{"version":1,"name":"Ohio Grade 6 · 6.EE unit review","difficulty":"advanced","pace":"practice","questions":[{"text":"Evaluate 3^3.","answers":["28","54","26","27"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Evaluate the exponent before adding.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.EE.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"power","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 6 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=42","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"6.EE.1","grade":6,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"power","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Whole-number exponents","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Evaluate 4 + 3^4.","answers":["84","85","86","170"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Evaluate the exponent before adding.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.EE.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"order-of-operations","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 6 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=42","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"6.EE.1","grade":6,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"order-of-operations","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Whole-number exponents","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Mina says 4³ means 4 × 3. Which explanation corrects her?","answers":["The exponent counts three factors: 4 × 4 × 4","Mina is correct for every base","The exponent means add 3 to the base","The exponent means divide the base by 3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"An exponent counts equal factors, not a multiplier applied once.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.EE.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"exponent-misconception","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 6 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=42","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"6.EE.1","grade":6,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"exponent-misconception","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Whole-number exponents","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"A code has three positions. Each position can use any of 2 symbols, and symbols may repeat. How many codes are possible?","answers":["7","16","9","8"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Multiply the number of choices for the three independent positions.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.EE.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"exponent-context","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 6 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=42","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"6.EE.1","grade":6,"version":"2017","so